[Id "caro-kann"]
[Name "Caro-Kann Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[ECO "B10-B19"]
[Description "Rock-solid defence: 1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5, with the light-squared bishop developed outside the pawn chain."]
[Tags "solid, beginner-friendly"]

1. e4 c6 {…c6 prepares …d5 and keeps the c8 bishop's path open, unlike the French.} 2. d4
  (2. Nc3 {@variation Two Knights} 2... d5 3. Nf3 Bg4 {…Bg4 pins the f3 knight, which helps White control e5 and d4.} 4. h3 Bxf3 {…Bxf3 gives the bishop pair but leaves Black with a very solid pawn structure.} 5. Qxf3 e6 {…e6 builds a pawn chain on light squares, where White's bishop can't attack it.} 6. d3 Nf6
{@line id=caro-kann-two-knights level=2 tier=side name="Two Knights (2.Nc3 3.Nf3)" summary="Trade the bishop for the f3 knight, then build a solid light-square pawn wall with …e6 and …d5."}
)
2... d5 3. e5 {@variation Advance}
  (3. Nc3 {@variation Classical} 3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 {…Bf5 develops with tempo on the e4 knight.} 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 {…h6 keeps a retreat square for the bishop, so h5 doesn't trap it.} 7. Nf3 Nd7 {…Nd7 stops Ne5 and prepares …Ngf6 without allowing a pawn-breaking Nxf6+.} 8. h5 Bh7 {…Bh7 keeps the bishop alive on its diagonal; White has spent time on h-pawn moves.}
{@line id=caro-kann-classical-main level=1 tier=main name="Classical (4…Bf5)" summary="Bishop to f5, then g6 and h7: answer the h-pawn march with …h6 and keep the bishop."}
9. Bd3 Bxd3 {…Bxd3 trades the good bishop for White's; Black's position is solid but a little passive.} 10. Qxd3 e6 {…e6 opens the f8 bishop; the black king will castle short or stay in the centre.} 11. Bd2 Ngf6 {…Ngf6 develops the last knight, eyeing e4 and g4.} 12. O-O-O Be7 {…Be7 prepares …O-O; the h5 pawn can become a target later.}
{@line id=caro-kann-classical-deep level=2 tier=main name="11.Bd2" summary="Trade light-squared bishops, then develop quietly with …e6, …Ngf6 and …Be7."}
)
  (3. exd5 cxd5 {…cxd5 gives Black the half-open c-file for the queenside play.} 4. Bd3 {@variation Exchange}
    (4. c4 {@variation Panov Attack} 4... Nf6 {…Nf6 hits d5 and develops; White aims for an isolated d-pawn position.} 5. Nc3 e6 {…e6 supports d5 and opens the f8 bishop.} 6. Nf3 Be7 7. cxd5 Nxd5 {…Nxd5 puts the knight on a strong central square in front of White's isolated pawn.} 8. Bd3 Nc6 9. O-O O-O
{@line id=caro-kann-panov level=1 tier=side name="Panov Attack (4.c4)" summary="Against the isolated d-pawn, blockade d5 with a knight and trade pieces."}
)
4... Nc6 5. c3 Nf6 6. Bf4 Bg4 {…Bg4 develops the bishop actively before …e6 locks it in.} 7. Qb3 Qd7 {…Qd7 defends b7 along the seventh rank.} 8. Nd2 e6 {…e6 opens the f8 bishop; next come …Bd6 and castling.}
{@line id=caro-kann-exchange-main level=1 tier=main name="Exchange Variation" summary="Develop the bishop to g4 before …e6, guard b7 with …Qd7, then play on the c-file."}
9. Ngf3 Bd6 {…Bd6 challenges White's good bishop on f4.} 10. Bxd6 Qxd6 {…Qxd6 recaptures and keeps the queen central.} 11. O-O O-O {…O-O: next Black plays on the queenside with …Rab8 and …b5.}
{@line id=caro-kann-exchange-deep level=2 tier=side name="9.Ngf3" summary="Trade dark-squared bishops, castle, then push …b5-b4 on the queenside (a minority attack)."}
)
3... Bf5 {…Bf5 develops the bishop outside the chain before …e6 shuts it in.} 4. Nf3
  (4. Bd3 Bxd3 {…Bxd3 swaps off Black's problem bishop, the usual worry in French-type structures.} 5. Qxd3 e6 6. Nf3 Qb6 {…Qb6 eyes d4 and b2.} 7. O-O c5 {…c5 strikes at the base of the chain.} 8. c3 Nc6
{@line id=caro-kann-advance-bd3 level=2 tier=main name="4.Bd3" summary="4.Bd3 lets you trade your bad bishop; then the French plan with …Qb6, …c5 and …Nc6."}
)
4... e6 5. Be2 c5 {…c5 hits d4, the base of White's pawn chain, as in the French.} 6. Be3 {Be3 defends d4, but the bishop no longer guards b2.}
  (6. O-O Nc6 {…Nc6 adds a second attacker on d4.}
{@line id=caro-kann-advance-oo level=1 tier=side name="Short, 6.O-O" summary="Against 6.O-O, develop with …Nc6 and keep hitting d4."}
7. c3 cxd4 {…cxd4 opens the c-file for Black's rook.} 8. cxd4 Nge7 {…Nge7 develops the last minor piece and keeps the f-pawn free for a later …f6 break.}
{@line id=caro-kann-advance-deep level=2 tier=side name="Short, 6.O-O and 7.c3" summary="Open the c-file with …cxd4 and pile up on d4 with your knights."}
)
6... Qb6 {…Qb6 hits b2 and adds a second attacker on d4.}
  (6... cxd4 {@alt})
{@line id=caro-kann-advance-main level=1 tier=main name="Short System" summary="Get the bishop out to f5 first, then …e6, …c5 and …Qb6 to hit d4 and b2."} *
